        <mxCell id="edge-next-extend" value="&lt;&lt;extend&gt;&gt; [Not Resolved; user requests guidance]" edge="1" parent="1" source="uc-next-steps" target="uc-handle-incidents" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;dashed=1;endArrow=open;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4776A8;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#203B5C;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" ><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-safety" value="&lt;b&gt;Automatic system behavior&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The system continuously monitors Smoke, Indoor / Outdoor Temperature, Water Leak, Door, Motion, Power and Internet / Connection. Outdoor temperature activates or deactivates cold-weather protection; Indoor Temperature and Power are mandatory while it is active, then prior user choices are restored. When attention is required, the system creates one Incident and updates that same history record if it escalates, resolves or closes. A Warning upgraded to Critical remains the same Incident.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Safety and escalation rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Smoke and Internet / Connection are always mandatory. Critical thresholds and notifications override normal settings. The owner is notified first; if there is no response, the system-set severity wait determines escalation. Warnings may go to configured contacts but never Emergency Services. Critical Incidents may escalate from contact to Emergency Services, directly if no contact is configured, or immediately when danger overrides normal waits. HOME / AWAY mainly affects Door and Motion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;No CO sensor, camera or external Weather Service. Physical sensors, backend, battery backup, Cellular / SIM, calls, SMS and emergency integrations are conceptual only." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;spacing=10;fillColor=#FFF8E8;strokeColor=#C77B24;fontColor=#513718;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="980" width="1080" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
